This sample shows how to call GetTcbBaselineAsync.

Uri endpoint = new Uri("<endpoint>");
TokenCredential credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
TcbBaselines client = new AttestationClient(endpoint, credential).GetTcbBaselinesClient(apiVersion: "2025-06-01");

Response<TcbBaselineResult> response = await client.GetTcbBaselineAsync(AttestationType.SgxEnclave);

This sample shows how to call GetTcbBaseline.

Uri endpoint = new Uri("<endpoint>");
TokenCredential credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
TcbBaselines client = new AttestationClient(endpoint, credential).GetTcbBaselinesClient(apiVersion: "2025-06-01");

Response<TcbBaselineResult> response = client.GetTcbBaseline(AttestationType.SgxEnclave);

This sample shows how to call GetTcbBaselineAsync and parse the result.

Uri endpoint = new Uri("<endpoint>");
TokenCredential credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
TcbBaselines client = new AttestationClient(endpoint, credential).GetTcbBaselinesClient(apiVersion: "2025-06-01");

Response response = await client.GetTcbBaselineAsync("SgxEnclave");

JsonElement result = JsonDocument.Parse(response.ContentStream).RootElement;
Console.WriteLine(result.ToString());

